## Statement

Find the remainder of the division of $P(x)=x^{100}+x+1$ by $x^2-1$.

## Hint

The remainder has degree at most $1$. Evaluate $P$ at the roots of $x^2-1$.

## Solution

Write $P(x)=(x^2-1)Q(x)+ax+b$, where $a,b$ are real numbers.

Evaluating at $x=1$ gives $P(1)=3=a+b$. Evaluating at $x=-1$ gives $P(-1)=1-1+1=1=-a+b$.

Adding the two equations gives $2b=4$, so $b=2$ and $a=1$. The remainder is $x+2$.
